p('<b>Question answered.</b> Yes: useful spectral-replacement existence is proved by the degree-corrected fourth moment on an explicit sparse family; useful incidence-conditioned replacement existence is also proved beyond B1. The original Proposition5.1 useful-parameter question remains answered negatively. <b>Limit.</b> The spectral obstruction is an unbounded family result for the specified shared data, not universal impossibility on all other classes. <b>Next bounded follow-up.</b> Construct or obstruct sparse scalar QC families in the useful nonzero-excess regime of the checked quantitative criterion, or determine sharp stopping distances for the general powers families. Neither is required to finish the positive existence answers.')

